WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.690
Why is South Korea's government making BTS
serve in the military?

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:07.140
I mean, yeah, it's required under South Korean
law that able-bodied men serve in the military

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.140
for two years.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.000
But I mean, come on they’re BTS.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.661
Famous people are always able to like pull
strings and like get out of stuff like this.

00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:14.661
Right?

00:00:14.661 --> 00:00:15.661
Not in this case.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:18.910
The head of the military manpower department
said that it would be, quote, “desirable”

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.710
for them to serve in the name of fairness.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:24.180
They’re trying to, like, lay a precedent
like, hey, everyone needs to serve, including

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.180
the rich and famous.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.180
No one is exempt, which I guess that's fair.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.180
Literally.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.060
And yeah, we all hate the rich people who
get out of doing what we all have to do.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.060
But in this case, it's different.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.060
When polled, South Koreans say that they're
actually in favor of giving BTS an exemption.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.060
They're like a national treasure.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.350
They’ve brought so much prestige and attention
and revenue and tourism to this country.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.940
But on the other hand, you've got to kind
of set a precedent here.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.780
South Korea's military has been running low
on service members, mainly because of dropping

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.780
birth rates.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.309
And by dropping birth rates, I mean the lowest
fertility rate on Earth.

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:48.309
In 2020, more people died than were born,
so their population actually went down.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:49.309
Korea’s government is trying to lower the
physical and mental standards for people to

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:50.309
enlist, but perhaps this is a good idea.

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:53.750
Let BTS serve in the military and re-energize
people's view of military service.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.750
This would certainly have an effect on the
many men who avoid conscription through some

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.750
questionable methods like dumping their citizenship.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.750
So actually, I don't have my mind made up
on this.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:57.750
This is a debate about fairness, about military
service, about the economy of South Korea.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.750
What do you think?

00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.750
Should BTS have to serve in the military?

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:00.750
Is it worth it?

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:00.753
Let me know.

